  "query_preview": "..\nA fairly dry regime will continue for another day or so as moderate \nto fresh trade winds dominate the weather pattern. Shower and \nthunderstorm chances begin to increase for Guam and Rota late Sunday \nnight as a broad trade-wind trough, with embedded Invest 95W, begin \nto lift west-northwest toward the area. 95W will gradually meander \nand wobble to the southwest of the Marianas through midweek as a \nbroad disorganized disturbance, with convergence along its northern \nperiphery inviting a slightly more unsettled pattern for the \nsouthernmost islands. There is uncertainty regarding timing and \nlocation of showers, as the movement of 95W will be affected by the \npath of TS Hagupit as it dissipates over the Philippine Sea, with \nmodels depicting some complex interactions between the remnants of \nHagupit, 95W, and a broad frontal system farther north. For the time \nbeing, a generally more unsettled pattern is expected to bring \nperiods of low-end scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms, \nmainly around Guam and Rota, from around Sunday night through at \nleast Tuesday.",
